{"tool_name":"linkedimm","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"linkedimm","home":"http://linkedimm.org","license":"Not licensed","summary":"A linked data graph database for integrating immunological data.","addition_date":"2022-01-14T15:45:30.300631Z","last_update_date":"2022-01-14T15:46:21.733598Z","tool_type":["Database portal","Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:linkedimm","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"kei.cheung@yale.edu","name":"Kei-Hoi Cheung","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Jeff Mandell"},{"name":"Shrikant Pawar"},{"name":"Steven H. Kleinstein"},{"name":"Syed Ahmad Chan Bukhari"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Data retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2422"},{"term":"Database search","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2421"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"LinkedImm","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S12859-021-04031-9","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Background: Many systems biology studies leverage the integration of multiple data types (across different data sources) to offer a more comprehensive view of the biological system being studied. While SQL (Structured Query Language) databases are popular in the biomedical domain, NoSQL database technologies have been used as a more relationship-based, flexible and scalable method of data integration. Results: We have created a graph database integrating data from multiple sources. In addition to using a graph-based query language (Cypher) for data retrieval, we have developed a web-based dashboard that allows users to easily browse and plot data without the need to learn Cypher. We have also implemented a visual graph query interface for users to browse graph data. Finally, we have built a prototype to allow the user to query the graph database in natural language. Conclusion: We have demonstrated the feasibility and flexibility of using a graph database for storing and querying immunological data with complex biological relationships. Querying a graph database through such relationships has the potential to discover novel relationships among heterogeneous biological data and metadata.","authors":[{"name":"Bukhari S.A.C."},{"name":"Cheung K.-H."},{"name":"Kleinstein S.H."},{"name":"Mandell J."},{"name":"Pawar S."}],"date":"2021-08-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"BMC Bioinformatics","title":"LinkedImm: a linked data graph database for integrating immunological data"},"pmcid":"PMC8385794","pmid":"34433410"}],"topic":[{"term":"Allergy, clinical immunology and immunotherapeutics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3400"},{"term":"Immunology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0804"},{"term":"Natural language processing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0218"},{"term":"Ontology and terminology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0089"},{"term":"Vaccinology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3966"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"LinkedImm","home":"https://bio.tools/linkedimm","license":"Not licensed","summary":"A linked data graph database for integrating immunological data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:linkedimm/db/linkedimm.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":2,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":1,"year":"2023"}],"doi":"10.1186/s12859-021-04031-9","pmcid":"PMC8385794","pmid":"34433410","ref_count":19,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2011"},{"count":1,"year":"2013"},{"count":1,"year":"2014"},{"count":2,"year":"2003"},{"count":2,"year":"20